## Security Considerations

The remote access design avoids directly exposing internal services to the public Internet.

The following systems remain on private internal addressing:

```text
ESXi Management: 10.10.99.21
DC01:             10.10.20.10
Linux Server:     10.10.20.20
```

Remote access is provided through the Tailscale overlay network instead of configuring public port forwarding for services such as:

- ESXi management
- SSH
- SMB
- Active Directory
- DNS

This reduces the need to expose management services directly to the Internet.

---

## Network Integration

The Tailscale subnet router is part of the existing physical and virtual network.

```text
Remote Device
     |
     v
Tailscale
     |
     v
Linux File Server
10.10.20.20
     |
     v
Servers-VLAN20
     |
     v
VMware ESXi
     |
     v
SW2 Gi1/0/13
     |
     v
Cisco Network
     |
     v
Internal Resources
```

The Linux server therefore acts as the bridge between the remote Tailscale network and the internal server VLAN.

