## Key Takeaway

Tailscale extended remote access into the homelab without requiring internal services to be exposed directly to the Internet.

Using the Linux File Server as a subnet router allowed remote systems to reach internal resources on `10.10.20.0/24` while keeping the existing Cisco VLAN and routing design intact.

The DNS testing also demonstrated an important troubleshooting concept: successful IP connectivity does not automatically mean DNS is configured correctly.

This setup provides a practical example of securely accessing private infrastructure while preserving internal network segmentation.
